# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EcoCycle Frontend — Environment Variables Template
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# .env is git-ignored. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# CURRENT STATUS:
#   The frontend is a fully client-side React/Vite SPA.
#   It uses no backend API and no server-side environment variables.
#   All persistence is handled in the browser via localStorage.
#   No VITE_* variables are required to run the application in this phase.
#
# FUTURE (Oracle Database integration):
#   When the Node.js/Express backend is added, the following variables
#   will be needed in backend/.env (NOT in this file):
#
#     ORACLE_USER=your_db_username
#     ORACLE_PASSWORD=your_db_password
#     ORACLE_CONNECTION_STRING=your_host:1521/your_service_name
#     JWT_SECRET=replace_with_a_long_random_string
#     PORT=5000
#     NODE_ENV=development
#
#   The frontend will then expose only:
#
#     VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# No variables are required for Phase 1 (frontend-only, localStorage).
# This file is intentionally minimal. Add entries here when the backend is introduced.

